/*
 * Core internal modules — the eight slots every hull must fill.
 *
 * The `standard` slice of Frontier's outfitting registry: core internal modules (armour, power plant, thrusters, FSD, life support, power distributor, sensors, fuel tank).
 *
 * Source:  EDCD FDevIDs, outfitting.csv
 *          https://github.com/EDCD/FDevIDs
 *          Community-maintained Frontier id/name registry. No explicit licence
 *          is stated; consult the repository terms.
 *
 * Each record is { symbol, category, name, mount?, guidance?, ship?, class,
 * rating, entitlement? }. `symbol` is the internal identifier
 * (e.g. `Hpt_PulseLaser_Fixed_Small`); `name` the display
 * name. `class` is the module size (0-8) and `rating` its grade letter (A-I) — the
 * "5A" the outfitting screen shows. `mount` (Fixed / Gimballed / Turreted) and
 * `guidance` (Dumbfire / Seeker / Swarm) appear only on the hardpoints they apply
 * to; `ship` names the hull an armour variant belongs to; `entitlement` carries
 * Frontier's DLC/grant token when the module is gated.
 *
 * Full provenance: data/ships/SOURCES.md.
 */
